        "section_heading": "RESULTS",
        "ordinal": 0,
        "text": "A linear mixed model (LMM) analysis revealed significant differences between the treatment groups and WLCC in interaction with the three assessment times in SAD and FNE. A significant reduction of both CBT + VRE and CBT + IE treatments on symptoms of SAD from pretreatment to posttreatment and 3 months follow-up (d pre-post = 1.31 and d pre-fu = 1.43 in CBT + VRE group; d pre-post = 1.90 and d pre-fu = 2.04 in CBT + IE group) and FNE (d pre-post = 1.35 and d pre-fu = 1.68 in the CBT + VRE group; d pre-post = 1.95 and d pre-fu = 1.59 in the CBT + IE group) compared to the WLCC was observed. No significant differences were observed between the VRE + CBT and CBT + IE groups on FNE. With respect to SAD, statistically significant between-group differences emerged in favour of the CBT + IE group, accompanied by substantial effect sizes at posttreatment (d = 0.87) and follow-up (d = 0.73).",
        "text_hash": "583777359fe220680385f12d0f2563098112c1c37ce403b24d40866a129d2da7",
